Subject: [PATCH] Name the encryption key's keychain item for Flux

Patch 0009 keeps the key for saved passwords and cookies in an item named
for the app embedding EngineCore. That app is Flux, so the item is named
for it. Flux built on CEF kept the key in "Chromium Safe Storage", which
0009 carries over, so existing profiles stay readable.
---
diff --git a/components/os_crypt/common/keychain_password_mac.mm b/components/os_crypt/common/keychain_password_mac.mm
--- a/components/os_crypt/common/keychain_password_mac.mm
+++ b/components/os_crypt/common/keychain_password_mac.mm
@@ -35,8 +35,8 @@
 const char kDefaultServiceName[] = "Chrome Safe Storage";
 const char kDefaultAccountName[] = "Chrome";
 #else
-const char kDefaultServiceName[] = "Sailfish Safe Storage";
-const char kDefaultAccountName[] = "Sailfish";
+const char kDefaultServiceName[] = "Flux Safe Storage";
+const char kDefaultAccountName[] = "Flux";
 #endif
 
 // The item the embedder's earlier builds kept the key in, under Chromium's
